I have a few Ideas for new classes. What do you people think.

1) Ranger: Stealth, and Alertness, has a knowledge of what is edable. Has 
a small chance of taming cats and dogs without food. Can find out the 
condition  of his or her pets. Starts with bow, sword (short or long), 
leather armor and some food rations. May be know more about some monsters.

2) Bard: Starts with an instrument (new instruments could be created if 
the others seem to usefull). Uses extended command #sobber_up to shake off 
confusion created by booze. Has a greater chance of ussing any instrument 
properly. May play a song at alter of Bridget (the goddes of bards), once 
per level and it will act as a sacrafice of worth coresponding to a random 
role. A low role means the bard screwed up. If this is attempted a second 
time before the bard rises in level you could get a message like "Bridget 
still remembers the song from the last time you played it, she wants you 
to learn a new one."

3) Scribe: Starts with a magic marker and blank scrools. Has a percent 
chance of identifying scrolls, but can't determine weather they are cursed 
or not.

4) Alchemist: Has a percent chance of identifying potions. Is more likely 
to have good effects when mixing potions, or is able to predict the result 
beforehand. Starts with a lot of potions.

5) Gypsy: Starts with magic jewelry of some sort. Has a chance of 
identifying objects as cursed. They can't weather something is blessed or not.
Have high charisma.

6) Cop: Starts with a wand of magic missles (six charges), a club +1, 
leather armor, and some dougnuts. Will not be attacted by Keystone Cops, 
and is less likely to be harmed by shopkeepers.

7) Psychic: Has a built in ring of warning, works like a crystal ball when 
s/he is hallucinating. Not much else.


